It is argued that the four  sub-components of proportionality are required to be satisfied, which  include:
 (a) A measure restricting a right must have a legitimate goal  (legitimate goal stage);
 (b) It must be a suitable means of furthering this goal (suitability or  rationale connection stage);
 (c) There must not be any less restrictive but equally effective  alternative (necessity stage); and  (d) The measure must not have a disproportionate impact on the  right holder (balancing stage).
